1
00:00:01,208 --> 00:00:04,666
Part One: Nutrition Challenges

2
00:00:05,083 --> 00:00:08,750
No matter how complete your diet
and caloric intake is,

3
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:12,250
you will likely still lose weight
throughout your treatment due

4
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:15,291
to side effects caused by radiation exposure.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
The first challenge to nutrition,
from radiation treatment

6
00:00:19,041 --> 00:00:22,208
to the head and neck is the loss of taste.

7
00:00:22,791 --> 00:00:26,166
This side effect will last
the entirety of treatment,

8
00:00:26,166 --> 00:00:29,000
and it will take several months to fully
come back,

9
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
potentially up to six months or more.

10
00:00:32,291 --> 00:00:35,625
Being unable to taste foods
the way you could before

11
00:00:35,625 --> 00:00:38,875
will decrease your appetite
and desire to eat.

12
00:00:39,583 --> 00:00:43,958
The second challenge is swelling
or irritation of the mucosa

13
00:00:43,958 --> 00:00:47,250
or lining of the head
and neck, caused by radiation.

14
00:00:47,875 --> 00:00:50,625
This effect is called mucositis.

15
00:00:50,833 --> 00:00:54,625
Mucositis,
or inflammation of the sensitive mucosa

16
00:00:54,875 --> 00:00:58,000
lining the mouth and esophagus will occur.

17
00:00:58,416 --> 00:01:03,166
The esophagus is the tube carrying food
from your mouth down to your stomach.

18
00:01:03,666 --> 00:01:07,958
Inflammation of these tissues is painful
and can make it more difficult

19
00:01:07,958 --> 00:01:09,833
to chew and swallow food.

20
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:14,250
These two issues are the main challenges to good nutrition

21
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:16,666
throughout head and neck radiation treatment.

22
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:20,416
Other possible setbacks include nausea.

23
00:01:20,625 --> 00:01:24,250
If you are receiving chemotherapy
in conjunction with radiation

24
00:01:24,791 --> 00:01:26,750
or recent surgical procedures

25
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:30,041
that make it more difficult
to physically swallow food.

26
00:01:30,541 --> 00:01:34,375
Unfortunately,
these challenges are unavoidable,

27
00:01:35,625 --> 00:01:38,583
but there are actions you can 
take to make your treatment

28
00:01:38,583 --> 00:01:43,708
and journey towards being cancer free
as smooth and painless as possible.

29
00:01:43,708 --> 00:01:46,750
This includes avoiding spicy foods,

30
00:01:46,750 --> 00:01:51,416
acidic or sour foods
such as orange juice and alcohol.

31
00:01:51,958 --> 00:01:54,583
These foods and liquids will irritate
and burn

32
00:01:54,583 --> 00:01:58,083
the already
irritated tissues of the throat and mouth.
